  "body": "Found while fixing #80. Axial drilling has a check that convicts a path cutting past the finished surface (drilling::axial_warnings). Cross (radial) drilling has none: on a solid bar with no modelled hole, a cross drill posts a hole the finished part does not have, and a cross hole deeper than the modelled hole is not caught either - the reach (#84), spindle (#62) and rapid (#77/#79) checks don't judge depth against the part.\n\nDone means: a cross drill whose hole is not in the model, or whose depth runs past the modelled hole into the finished part, is refused by name (verify's radial mode or the cross arm); pinned by a solid bar with no hole (refused) and a bar with a modelled cross hole drilled to its depth (posts).",
